-- importpromote.lind — import-position promotion (§13.25): both
-- bytestring positions of `import` take "..." literals. Each desugars
-- at parse time to bytesBind AutoN + import —
--   bytesBind Auto0 (103, ...); bytesBind Auto1 (95, ...);
--   import Auto0 Auto1 []
-- the fwrite-promotion precedent (§13.24), no manual handle+bind
-- dance. The desugared form is what `--parse` renders (fixed point).
-- The (Imported, H, suffix) completion tuple carries the handle AS
-- WRITTEN — the anonymous Auto0 — so the consumer gates on a
-- distinctive suffix: "" would be indistinguishable from the prelude's
-- (Imported, Prelude, "") tuple. Standalone: run with
-- `lindana examples/importpromote.lind`, exit 0.
: import "greeter" "_v2" []
(Imported, nh, "_v2") : (Greet_v2, "world", Outbox)
Outbox {
  (Hello_v2, who) : [say "promoted import says: hello, %s" who; exit 0]
}
